        "count": 18,
        "start": 1
      },
      "vo": "In 1902, snow fell on a New York streetcar, so the driver kept stopping to wipe the glass by hand."
    },
    {
      "primitive": "highlighter-swipe",
      "transition": "ink-wipe",
      "params": {
        "text": "In *1903*, *Mary Anderson* patented the wiper."
      },
      "vo": "But in 1903, Mary Anderson won US patent 743,801 for a lever that swept a rubber blade."
    },
    {
      "primitive": "conveyor",
      "transition": "cut",
      "params": {
        "item": {
